/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/N2H5-formation.dat -- a protonation of hydrazine, written from the master:
      Hydrazine + H+  <=>  N2H5
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv.

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = -0.99, dH1 = 38.1 kJ/mol (grade CC)
      pK2 = 8.02, dH2 = 41.7 kJ/mol (grade BB)
  Source: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231; standard state: hypothetical ideal solution of unit molality, 298.15 K, 0.1 MPa (Section 8, p. 359).
  The master is Hydrazine, the form a case declares; this record carries step 2 (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
  The neutral base is `Hydrazine`, not `N2H4`: the catalogue holds a component N2H4, a derived neutral species of that name would have to carry the `aq` suffix, and check_species_identity pins that suffix as a closed historical class (so `N2H4aq` is refused).  The master is the neutral base `Hydrazine` (the compound as weighed), and the records protonate it.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species N2H5; masters ( { ion Hydrazine; nu 1; } { ion H; nu 1; } );
      logK25 8.02; dH -41700; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 -- Section 8 summary, p. 360, and Section 7.40, p. 300: pK2 8.02, dH2 41.7 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
